caption: Tradition Paths
tradition-component: tradition-paths

An Innovator may purchase exactly one of the following 20-point Tradition Paths. The Paths are permanently mutually exclusive: a character may never purchase or benefit from more than one, even after mastering Innovator.

Spellwright (20 points): While personally leading an Occult spell-invention project, you may bind ordinary Insight to that project before it expires, turning it into Project Insight. In addition, any natural critical success on a Concept roll, prototyping roll, or other roll that is part of that invention generates 1 Project Insight. Project Insight is tied to that project, does not count against your normal Insight limit, and does not expire while the project remains active; you may hold no more Project Insight for one project than your Magery. Before an invention or prototyping roll for that project, you may spend 1 Project Insight for Precision or Breakthrough as though it were ordinary Insight; Efficiency has no effect on invention. After the spell is successfully prototyped, you may spend remaining Project Insight to clean the design before finalizing it: 1 Project Insight removes one minor bug, while 2 Project Insight downgrades one major bug to a minor bug; removing that remaining minor bug costs 1 additional Project Insight. The GM applies these expenditures to the actual hidden bug list. This Path applies to any Occult spell-invention project you are legally allowed to perform, not only Foundational spells. All ordinary invention time, laboratory, prerequisite, prototype, and failure rules still apply.

Metamagician (20 points): You may purchase Metamagic Principles. To buy a Principle, choose one Enhancement and, if it is leveled, a maximum level or modifier; you must already have fully bought off that Enhancement technique for at least one spell at that level. The Principle costs five times the character points required to fully buy off that spell-enhancement technique at the chosen modifier. Once purchased, you may apply that Enhancement, up to the purchased maximum, as a fully bought-off technique to any spell you can cast for which Adjustable Spells permits that Enhancement. This does not make an invalid Enhancement legal, create a parameter or function the spell does not possess, or remove the Enhancement's extra energy cost, casting consequences, or other requirements. Lower levels of a leveled Enhancement are included; the Principle may later be upgraded by paying the difference between its old and new costs.

Reconstructor (20 points): When you personally observe a discrete Occult magical effect being performed, you may analyze it with Thaumatology. A successful Thaumatology roll is required before you may reconstruct that effect; Insight may be spent on this roll normally. On success, you may translate the observed effect into Innovator Ritual Magic under the following rules. Ordinary Tier 2 spell magic needs no special reconstruction beyond Innovator's normal College-and-technique access. For an Occult Magic Talent or other Occult Talented effect, each source Power Talent becomes one Reconstructed College; a successfully analyzed ability may be learned as a Hard technique of that College, with a default penalty of -1 per 5 character points of the reproduced active effect, rounded up. For Tier 3 Realm, Word, and other effect-producing Occult Traditions, create one or more Reconstructed Colleges with approximately the same conceptual breadth as the Realm, noun, or equivalent scope-bearing element used by the source effect. If several such elements are genuinely required, the reconstructed technique defaults from the lowest applicable College. A Tier 3 reconstructed effect is a Hard technique whose penalty magnitude equals the source effect's own skill penalty plus the source caster's margin of success for the observed working. Its energy cost equals the source effect's energy cost, and any mandatory nonenergy requirement intrinsic to producing that fixed effect also remains. Reconstructed Colleges are closed: they grant no improvisational authority and permit only specific effects successfully reconstructed through this Path. Reconstructing an effect never grants the source Tradition, Realm levels, Words, Power Talents, flexible construction rules, Mastery permissions, character-point generation, ascension procedures, access grants, or other metaprogression. You reproduce only the fixed effect you successfully analyzed.
